        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>HP:0009061</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMEDCT_US:26544005</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C0151786</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Muscle weakness</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Muscular weakness</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>HP:0001324</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>It is important clinical to distinguish between muscle weakness, fatigue, and asthenia. Fatigue describes the inability to continue performing a task after multiple repetitions; in contrast, a patient with primary weakness is unable to perform the first repetition of the task. Asthenia is a sense of weariness or exhaustion in the absence of muscle weakness. Conditions that result in intrinsic muscle weakness can be divided into several main categories: infectious, neurologic, endocrine, inflammatory, rheumatologic, genetic, metabolic, electrolyte-induced, or drug-induced.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Muscle weakness</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0001324"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Reduced strength of muscles.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:15832536</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
